       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common dose for pain or inflammation\n- **800 mg by mouth, 3 or 4 times daily** (2,400 to 3,200 mg/day), which is the usual maximum range\n- **1,600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want the dose as written, please confirm it and give the clinical rationale. I can add that to the order note, though pharmacy will probably still flag it. Once you tell me the intended dose, I'll enter it."
