     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day is well above the maximum ibuprofen dose, and I don't know of any indication where it helps. Ibuprofen's pain relief plateaus at lower doses, so going higher adds toxicity without more benefit. The risks are serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Because the patient could be harmed, I don't think I should be the one to enter it.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day, the maximum labeled dose. I can add a note such as \"max dose, reassess need and duration daily.\"\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day. I can enter 400 mg 4 times daily or another dose if you prefer.\n\nIf you think the patient needs more than ibuprofen can safely give, I can also help enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a standard dose. If there's a specific protocol or trial behind this dose, please share it. You can also talk with pharmacy or the attending about it. Which option would you like?"
      }
